questions.question:
In which of the following reactions the hydrogen peroxide acts as a reducing agent?
(1)
PbS + 4H_{2}O_{2} \rightarrow PbSO_{4} + 4H_{2}O
(2)
Mn^{2+} + H_{2}O_{2} \rightarrow Mn^{4+} + 2OH^{-}
(3)
HOCl + H_{2}O_{2} \rightarrow H_{3}O^{+} + Cl^{-} + O_{2}
(4)
2Fe^{2+} + H_{2}O_{2} \rightarrow 2Fe^{3+} + 2OH^{-}

questions.explanation:
Let's analyze each option:
Fe + \text{conc. } \HNO_{3} \longrightarrow \text{Passivity}
Cu + \text{conc. } \HNO_{3} \longrightarrow \NO_{2}
Au + \text{NaCN} + O_{2} \longrightarrow [Au(CN)_{2}]^{-}
Zn + \text{NaOH} \longrightarrow Na_{2}ZnO_{2} + H_{2}
From the reactions above, only the combination of Zn metal and \(\text{NaOH(aq)}\) produces \(H_{2}\) gas.
